WEBVTT

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:04.665
Node.js application security combines secure coding, dependency governance,

00:00:04.665 --> 00:00:10.020
runtime validation, access control, secrets management, safe file and process handling,

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:14.155
careful logging, and secure deployment practices. The platform is flexible and productive,

00:00:14.155 --> 00:00:18.000
but that flexibility means teams must be explicit about trust boundaries,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.000
runtime behavior, and operational controls.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.975
Strong Node.js security treats every boundary as untrusted.

00:00:22.975 --> 00:00:27.730
Requests, headers, cookies, files, environment configuration, package scripts,

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:31.980
third-party APIs, queue messages, logs, and deployment settings can all affect security.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.020
The application should validate data before business logic,

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.000
enforce authorization on the server, limit privileges,

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.980
and fail in ways that are safe and observable.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.980
Every dependency is a supply chain decision.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:45.028
Teams should understand direct and transitive dependencies, maintain lockfiles,

00:00:45.028 --> 00:00:47.980
review updates, use software composition analysis,

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.980
and prefer packages that are maintained and necessary. The point is not to fear npm.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.130
The point is to make dependency choices visible enough that speed does not erase

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:58.975
accountability. The goal is not to memorize every vulnerability.

00:00:58.975 --> 00:01:04.000
The goal is to build Node.js applications that are explicit, least-privileged, observable,

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.045
resilient, and safe to operate. When developers and operators share that mindset,

00:01:07.045 --> 00:01:10.990
security becomes part of normal engineering: clear contracts, careful defaults,

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:13.015
reliable deployment, useful monitoring,

00:01:13.015 --> 00:01:16.840
and defensive handling of the data and services the application touches.
